id: pm-http-a8z1
title: Track backend-owned conditional mutation capability
description: "Public CommitItemMutationsOptions and CommitWorkspaceTransactionOptions require pmRoot:string; ExtensionCommandSdk has no backend-owned conditional item mutation service. Upstream issue #1399 remains open. Remote reads use injected PmClient; writes and sends refuse before effects until the host offers this capability."
type: Task
status: open
priority: 2
tags[7]: "gh:unbraind/pm-cli#1399","gh:unbraind/pm-cli#1576","gh:unbraind/pm-cli#1620",sdk-gap,"upstream:pm-cli#1399","upstream:pm-cli#1576","upstream:pm-cli#1620"
created_at: "2026-10-28T23:41:25.429Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-29T05:59:59.163Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Adopt the public backend-owned conditional writer when released, then run the same concurrency and crash conformance suite against it."
parent: pm-http-76jn
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-29T05:59:49.861Z",codex-agent,"Related public SDK constraints confirmed in the pinned declarations and orchestrator notes: BulkItemUpdateMutation.match is keyed selection, not an item expected-revision precondition (#1576); workspace transactions do not exclude ordinary native writers (#1620). Package guards re-read before effects and preserve caller revision/native-source digest through recovery, but the re-read-to-send window remains. Cooperating package writers preserve response reservations; arbitrary native writers can ignore them."
body: ""
